[gd_scene load_steps=48 format=3]

; Tri-axle tanker semi-trailer. Hand-built low-poly (Kenney ships no trailers at all), boxes and
; 12-segment cylinders — the barrel is the one part in the trailer family that earns more than the
; kit's usual 10 segments, because it is the whole silhouette.
;
; AUTHORED WITH THE ORIGIN AT THE KINGPIN, ground at y = -1.05 — the family convention, measured
; off the tractor unit's fifth-wheel plate. See flatbed.tscn's header for why.
;
; THE BARREL STARTS AT z 1.05, NOT AT THE KINGPIN, and that is the gooseneck rule rather than a
; styling choice: a 0.85 m barrel centred at y 0.66 has its underside at y -0.19, which is BELOW
; the coupling plane. Run it forward over the tractor and it passes through the fifth wheel, the
; frame rails and the mudguards. So it stops behind the tractor's tail (z 0.96 in this frame) and
; the gooseneck carries a PUMP CABINET instead — which is what real tankers put there.
;
; MEASURED against the tractor unit: barrel 1.70 across (narrower than the 1.92 frame, as a tank
; is), 5.10 m long, top at y 1.51 and the handrail at 1.84 = 2.89 m above the road. Ground
; clearance under the barrel is 0.86 m, which clears the 0.36 m bogie wheels by 16 mm — the reason
; the barrel sits as high as it does, and the reason its centre of mass is the highest in the
; catalog (tanker_spec.tres).
;
; The parts, all of them recognisable rather than decorative: dished END CAPS proud of the shell,
; three RING STIFFENERS, three SADDLES carrying the barrel down onto the frame rails, a CATWALK
; with handrails and two MANLIDS in spill trays, two HOSE TUBES slung under the frame, and a REAR
; CABINET with its discharge pipe — the valve gear a tank trailer discharges through.
;
; Nothing here is a load model. The surge lives in tanker.gd, is LABELLED as a model rather than
; fluid dynamics, and reaches the world only by moving this body's centre of mass.
;
; Swing clearance: the frontmost part is the gooseneck at 0.33 m ahead of the kingpin and 0.96
; half-width, swinging on 1.02 m inside the 1.15 m to the cab's rear face. The pump cabinet is
; narrower and shorter, so it never becomes the frontmost part. test_trailer sweeps it.

